  ✓ Stage 2: check source/translation fidelity and run independent differential tests
  ✓ Stage 3: rebuild concrete/proof definitions from source and rerun every positive claim
  ✓ Stage 4: audit claim adequacy, real-program pinning, and concrete witnesses
  ✓ Stage 5: inventory and review every syntax/function/rule/attribute statically
  → Stage 6: build and run a fresh false result mutation
  • Stage 7: account for proven versus assumed facts and write the final review
